[# layout/asymmetric: an editorial two-column layout with unequal columns and the smaller one offset downward.

   The offset gives the layout its staggered look. On mobile the columns stack, main first.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: renders as a table row. The offset is a spacer, so it works.
   - Gmail apps: stacking works. Gmail on non-Google accounts shows the desktop layout on phones.
   - Dark mode: swaps via dm-* classes when on the brand surface or background color. #]
[% set offsetBlock %][[ c('layout/spacer', {}, { settings: { height: s.offset } }) ]][% endset %]
[% set aside = offsetBlock + data.aside %]
[% set splitReversed = s.split.split('/') | reverse | join('/') %]
[% if s.asidePosition == 'right' %]
[[ c('layout/columns', { columns: [data.main, aside] }, { settings: { split: s.split, valign: 'top', background: s.background, padding: s.padding, columnPadding: s.columnPadding, hideOnMobile: s.hideOnMobile, hideOnDesktop: s.hideOnDesktop } }) ]]
[% else %]
[[ c('layout/columns', { columns: [aside, data.main] }, { settings: { split: splitReversed, valign: 'top', background: s.background, padding: s.padding, columnPadding: s.columnPadding, mobileLayout: 'reverse', hideOnMobile: s.hideOnMobile, hideOnDesktop: s.hideOnDesktop } }) ]]
[% endif %]
